/*!
    \page project-structure.html
    \title Project Structure
    \previouspage Architecture
    \nextpage Troubleshooting

    This chapter is a map from \e{"where is X implemented?"} to the source tree. It is
    deliberately not an exhaustive file list; it points at the directory and the few key
    files for each area, each linking into the \l {OpcUaManager API Reference}.

    \section1 Top-level layout

    \table
    \header \li Directory \li Role
    \row \li \c app/ \li GUI executable: startup, QML engine wrapper, app services.
    \row \li \c src/ \li Reusable C++ libraries (client core, models, persistence, projects, facades).
    \row \li \c runtime/ \li Headless open62541 OPC UA server executable.
    \row \li \c qml/ \li Application QML module (screens/dialogs) and the \c qml/Base reusable module.
    \row \li \c resources/ \li Bundled images/SVG and QML style configuration.
    \row \li \c doc/ \li This documentation (QDoc manual pages, API topics, config).
    \row \li \c packaging/, \c installer/ \li Release pipeline, installer, and product metadata.
    \endtable

    \section1 Where each feature lives

    \table
    \header \li To work on… \li Look in… \li Key types
    \row \li Client connection / discovery / subscriptions
         \li \c src/core/opcuaservice.* \li \l OpcUaService
    \row \li The client object QML talks to
         \li \c src/qmlapi/opcuamanager.* \li \l OpcUaManager
    \row \li Address-space (browse) tree
         \li \c src/models/opcuamodel.*, \c treeitem.* \li \l OpcUaModel, \l TreeItem
    \row \li Node attributes / values / trends
         \li \c src/models/ \li \l AttributesModel, \l DataAccessModel, \l TrendModel
    \row \li Structured (CODESYS) value decoding
         \li \c src/core/structurednodereader.* \li \c StructuredNodeReader
    \row \li Server design + runtime control
         \li \c src/qmlapi/serverstudio.*, \c serverruntimecontroller.* \li \l ServerStudio, \l ServerRuntimeController
    \row \li Server project model / file / validation / NodeSet2
         \li \c src/serverproject/ \li \l{ServerProject}{ServerProject::*}
    \row \li The headless server itself
         \li \c runtime/ \li \c ProjectBuilder, \c SimulationEngine, \c SecuritySetup, \c DiagnosticsServer, \c RuleEngine
    \row \li Client project (\c .uaproj)
         \li \c src/project/ \li \l ProjectData, \c ProjectSerializer
    \row \li Monitored-node persistence
         \li \c src/persistence/nodedatabase.* \li \l NodeDatabase
    \row \li Installed/portable paths
         \li \c src/core/apppaths.* \li \l AppPaths
    \row \li App startup / services
         \li \c app/ \li \l AppCore, \l AppEngine, \l AppInfo, \l LocaleController
    \row \li UI shell and screens
         \li \c qml/Main.qml, \c qml/*Screen*.qml \li \l {OpcUaManager QML Types}
    \row \li Reusable UI controls
         \li \c qml/Base/ \li \l {Base QML Types}
    \endtable

    \section1 Libraries and their boundaries

    \list
        \li \b OpcUaCore (\c src/core, \c src/models, \c src/persistence, \c src/project)
            — the client stack; links Qt Core/Network/OpcUa/Sql.
        \li \b ServerProjectCore (\c src/serverproject) — \e{Qt Core only}, so it is shared
            by the GUI and the headless runtime.
        \li \b OpcUaQmlApi (\c src/qmlapi) — the QML facades; depends on both cores.
    \endlist

    For the reasoning behind these boundaries, threads, and processes, see \l {Architecture}.
*/
